Source: @PACKAGE@
Section: embedded
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               autoconf,
               automake,
               libtool,
               pkg-config,
               texinfo,
               libusb-1.0-0-dev,
               libftdi1-dev,
               libhidapi-dev,
               libjaylink-dev,
               libgpiod-dev,
               libcapstone-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools

Package: @PACKAGE@
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: openocd
Conflicts: openocd, openocd-rp1pio, @CONFLICTS@
Replaces: openocd, openocd-rp1pio, @CONFLICTS@
Description: OpenOCD with the fpgas.online patch series (@TRACK@)
 OpenOCD is the Open On-Chip Debugger: JTAG/SWD debugging, flashing and
 boundary-scan for embedded targets and FPGAs. This is the fpgas.online
 build of upstream @UPSTREAM_REF@ (commit @UPSTREAM_COMMIT@) plus a patch
 series that is not yet upstream:
  * rp1_pio_jtag adapter: JTAG through the Raspberry Pi 5 RP1 PIO block
    (librp1jtag, linked in statically) instead of bit-banging
    PCIe-attached GPIOs;
  * board/netv2-rpi*.cfg: the Kosagi NeTV2 on a Raspberry Pi header via
    bcm2835gpio (Pi 1-4), rp1_pio_jtag (Pi 5) or linuxgpiod, with a
    picker and a jtagspi configuration-flash variant;
  * fpga/lattice-ecp5-traceid.cfg: ECP5 TraceID read, next to upstream's
    fpga/xilinx-dna.cfg Device DNA read.
 .
 It installs /usr/bin/openocd and /usr/share/openocd in place of Debian's
 openocd package. The version @VERSION@ names the upstream base first and
 the fpgas.online patch-set revision after "+fpgasonline.".
